# Every message is one run. The FIRST message the page sends is
# {"type":"attach","cols":C,"rows":R}; parse it so the attach rule can read
# the geometry. Once the session is attached the chassis stops making runs
# for this socket — the terminal's frames go straight to the process — so
# this parse only ever sees the one attach message (and any the page sends
# after a detach).
WHEN @websocket.phase == "message" && @websocket.msg.text != ""
  EMIT .msg = &json(@websocket.msg.text)
